  "description": "LOSWEX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H84 N12 O58 Yb9 1+,4(C1 H4 O1),N1 O3 1-,3(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2A (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb3A (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb4A (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb5A (Yb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.458-5.129 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.57-167.83°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C59H88Yb9N13O65Cl6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
